-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008), §72: the existing principal's personal
-- percentage supplement — T, the March pay of his whole position; B = T ×
-- (100 + Y)%; C, the difference between B and the new table pay, turned
-- into a percentage of the combined salary; not pensionable, with
-- provident-fund contributions under the Dafna agreement.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `base-agreement-common`
IMPORT conventions

§ `72`

-- akn:art_72 The heading line: the personal percentage supplement of an existing principal on the move to the reform.

-- (א) ¶2–¶4: T, the pay of the whole position (not 100%) in the
-- determining month, without refunds, yearly payments, gross-up and
-- benefit; on unpaid leave or a sabbatical, the March before those
-- periods; on reserve duty or maternity leave, the pay he would have had at
-- the position of the month before.
@ref akn:art_72__para_a akn:art_72__para_a/p2 akn:art_72__para_a/p3 akn:art_72__para_a/p4
DECLARE `month T is taken from` IS ONE OF
    `March of the year before the move`
    `March of the year before the unpaid leave`

GIVEN `on unpaid leave or a sabbatical on the eve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `month T is taken from`
DECIDE `the month of T` `on unpaid leave or a sabbatical on the eve` IS
    IF `on unpaid leave or a sabbatical on the eve` THEN `March of the year before the unpaid leave` ELSE `March of the year before the move`

-- ¶5–¶8: B = T × (100 + Y)%; C is the difference between B and the new
-- table pay, turned into a percentage of the combined salary. The text
-- prints "C= שכר טבלאי חדש - B"; its two examples (§§74, 87) take B less
-- the table pay, and so does this rule. Never below nothing (convention
-- amounts.never-negative); no rounding is stated (convention
-- rounding.default).
@ref akn:art_72__para_a/p5 akn:art_72__para_a/p6 akn:art_72__para_a/p7 akn:art_72__para_a/p8
GIVEN t IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER, `new table pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the personal supplement rate` t y `new table pay` IS
    max 0 ((t TIMES (100 PLUS y) DIVIDED BY 100) MINUS `new table pay`) DIVIDED BY `new table pay`

-- (ב): not a permanent supplement for the budgetary pension, and no
-- accrual-pension contributions on it.
@ref akn:art_72__para_b
`the personal supplement is pensionable` MEANS FALSE

-- (ג): contributions to a non-paying provident fund "בגין התגמול כאמור
-- בפסקה (3)" — 13⅓% employer (8⅓% severance, 5% benefits), 5% employee,
-- by the Dafna agreement. F-ofek-hadash-base-72-a: §72 has no paragraph
-- (3); the words are §33(ד)(4)'s, written for hours beyond 100%. The
-- reading adopted (convention reading.misprint): the contributions are on
-- the personal supplement, the only payment §72 makes.
@ref akn:art_72__para_c
`the employer's contribution on the personal supplement` MEANS 40/3 DIVIDED BY 100
`the employee's contribution on the personal supplement` MEANS 5%

`the numbered paragraphs of §72` MEANS LIST "(א)", "(ב)", "(ג)", "(ד)"
`72(ג) cites a paragraph (3) §72 does not have` MEANS
    NOT elem "(3)" `the numbered paragraphs of §72`
#ASSERT `72(ג) cites a paragraph (3) §72 does not have`

-- akn:art_72__para_d The undertaking to negotiate a clarification of section 3.ה of the agreement of 27.12.84 (as §33(ד)(5)); no rule.

-- §74's example: T = 15,000, Y = 15%, table 14,819: B = 17,250, C = 2,431,
-- 16.4% to the tenth. §87's: T = 12,000, Y × 0.8 = 12%, table 11,521: B =
-- 13,440, C = 1,919, which the text prints as 16.6% (16.656…%, cut at the
-- tenth; convention precedence.example — the rule's figure is exact).
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` (1000 TIMES `the personal supplement rate` 15000 15 14819) EQUALS 164
#ASSERT TRUNC (1000 TIMES `the personal supplement rate` 12000 12 11521) 0 EQUALS 166
